---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getArticleSchema, getBreadcrumbSchema } from '../config/site';

const title = "Security Architecture & Cryptographic Guarantees — SlingShare";
const description = "Comprehensive breakdown of the SlingShare security model: DTLS-SRTP end-to-end encryption, ephemeral room isolation, and zero server storage.";
const path = "/security";

const structuredData = [
  getArticleSchema(title, description, path),
  getBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Security", path: path },
  ]),
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={path} ogType="article" structuredData={structuredData}>
  <div class="article-page">
    <div class="container article-container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb-nav" aria-label="Breadcrumbs">
        <a href="/">Home</a> / <span>Security Model</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="article-header">
        <div class="badge badge-coral">Security Whitepaper</div>
        <h1>SlingShare Security Architecture</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          We treat privacy and security as non-negotiable fundamentals. Here is how SlingShare protects your data from eavesdropping, interception, and unauthorized access.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="article-body">
        <h2>1. Zero Server-Side File Storage</h2>
        <p>
          The SlingShare Go signaling server is physically incapable of storing files. It operates solely as a temporary WebSocket rendezvous hub for exchanging session metadata (SDP offers and ICE candidates).
        </p>
        <p>
          The WebSocket message parser implements a strict <strong>64 KB maximum message size</strong> limit. Any attempted transmission of binary files through the signaling server is automatically rejected by the server pipeline.
        </p>

        <h2>2. End-to-End Encryption (DTLS-SRTP)</h2>
        <p>
          All peer-to-peer data channels created by WebRTC are automatically encrypted using Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS).
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cryptographic Ciphers:</strong> Modern AES-GCM and ChaCha20-Poly1305 ciphers negotiated directly by browser engines.</li>
          <li><strong>Forward Secrecy:</strong> Ephemeral Diffie-Hellman key exchange ensures that past communications cannot be decrypted even if an encryption key were compromised in the future.</li>
          <li><strong>Immunity to Man-in-the-Middle:</strong> The signaling server only handles the initial SDP fingerprints, which are authenticated during the DTLS handshake.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Ephemeral Sessions & Unpredictable Identifiers</h2>
        <p>
          Room codes are generated using cryptographically secure random number generators (<code>crypto/rand</code> in Go) drawn from an alphabet that avoids visual ambiguity (omitting 0, O, 1, and I).
        </p>
        <p>
          Sessions are automatically garbage-collected and permanently purged when all peers disconnect or after reaching idle timeouts.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Cryptographic Integrity Verification (SHA-256)</h2>
        <p>
          Before any file is dispatched, the sending client computes a SHA-256 digest using the native W3C Web Crypto API. Upon receiving the final chunk, the receiving browser independently hashes the assembled bytes and validates the checksum before granting download access.
        </p>

        <div class="security-matrix card">
          <h3>Summary Security Matrix</h3>
          <div class="matrix-item">
            <strong>Where are files stored?</strong>
            <span>Only in the volatile memory of the sender and receiver devices. Never on the server.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="matrix-item">
            <strong>Can the server operator inspect transferred files?</strong>
            <span>No. Payloads are encrypted via DTLS before leaving the sender's browser.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="matrix-item">
            <strong>Are accounts or credentials stored?</strong>
            <span>No user accounts exist. Sessions are fully ephemeral.</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="article-cta card-dark">
          <h3>Experience privacy-first file transfer</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--color-on-dark-soft); margin: 8px 0 20px;">No account required. Protected by end-to-end encryption.</p>
          <a href="/app" class="btn btn-primary">Launch SlingShare</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .article-page { padding: var(--spacing-xxl) 0; }
  .article-container { max-width: 780px; }
  .breadcrumb-nav { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--color-muted); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg); }
  .article-header { margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl); }
  .article-header h1 { margin: var(--spacing-sm) 0 var(--spacing-md); }
  .article-body h2 { margin: var(--spacing-xl) 0 var(--spacing-sm); }
  .article-body p { margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md); line-height: 1.65; }
  .article-body ul { margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md); padding-left: 20px; line-height: 1.65; }
  .security-matrix { padding: var(--spacing-xl); background-color: var(--color-surface-soft); margin: var(--spacing-xl) 0; }
  .security-matrix h3 { margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md); }
  .matrix-item { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); padding: var(--spacing-sm) 0; }
  .matrix-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .matrix-item strong { display: block; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .matrix-item span { font-size: 0.925rem; color: var(--color-body); }
  .article-cta { margin-top: var(--spacing-xxl); padding: var(--spacing-xl); text-align: center; }
</style>
